oning\",\"content\":\"The `dep.calls == 1` — the rejected call still touched dep? No — `dep.calls` incremented... Ah, I see: the second call `await breaker.call(dep.call)` — `dep.call` is passed as a function. Even if `_try_acquire_permission` returns False, `dep.call` is never invoked, so dep.calls shouldn't increment. But dep.calls == 1...\\n\\nWait — the first failure test earlier: `with pytest.raises(ConnectionError): run(lambda: breaker.call(dep.call))` — dep.set_mode(\\\"fail\\\") and breaker.call(dep.call) invokes dep.call once, so dep.calls == 1 already from that first trip! Of course. So the assertion should be that the second call did NOT increment dep.calls. Let me record dep.calls before the rejected call: `calls_before = dep.calls` then after rejection assert `dep.calls == calls_before`.\\n\\nActually simpler: assert dep.calls == 1 (only from the trip call) and no additional calls from the scenario. Let me fix.\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:37.000Z\",\"endedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:38.000Z\",\"thinkingSeconds\":1},{\"type\":\"text\",\"content\":\"الخطأ بسيط: `dep.calls` عدّت استدعاء الإخفاق الأول الذي فتح الدائرة. أصلح التوكيد:\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:38.000Z\",\"endedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:39.000Z\"},{\"type\":\"credit_usage\",\"content\":10,\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:40.000Z\"},{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"content\":{\"id\":\"call_00_Glm8HoIsaGFeK4GEyTQ03433\",\"name\":\"edit_file\",\"args\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/daytona/asyncio_circuit_breaker/tests/test_circuit_breaker.py\",\"new_string\":\"    result = run(scenario)\\n    assert result == \\\"ok\\\"\\n    # نجاح المحاولة التجريبية أغلق الدائرة\\n    assert breaker.state is CircuitState.CLOSED\\n    # dep لم يُلمس إلا مرة واحدة فقط (استدعاء الفتح الأول)؛\\n    # المحاولة التجريبية استخدمت first_slow، والطلب الثاني رُفض قبل الوصول للخادم\\n    assert dep.calls == 1\",\"old_string\":\"    result = run(scenario)\\n    assert result == \\\"ok\\\"\\n    # نجاح المحاولة التجريبية أغلق الدائرة، والخادم لم يُلمس سوى مرة واحدة\\n    assert breaker.state is CircuitState.CLOSED\\n    assert dep.calls == 0\",\"__result\":\"Successfully replaced 1 instance(s) of the string in '/home/daytona/asyncio_circuit_breaker/tests/test_circuit_breaker.py'\"},\"result\":\"Successfully replaced 1 instance(s) of the string in '/home/daytona/asyncio_circuit_breaker/tests/test_circuit_breaker.py'\",\"hasResult\":true},\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:40.000Z\",\"endedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:42.000Z\"},{\"type\":\"tool_call_result\",\"content\":{\"tool_call_id\":\"call_00_Glm8HoIsaGFeK4GEyTQ03433\",\"name\":\"edit_file\",\"content\":\"Successfully replaced 1 instance(s) of the string in '/home/daytona/asyncio_circuit_breaker/tests/test_circuit_breaker.py'\"},\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:42.000Z\",\"endedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:42.000Z\"},{\"type\":\"credit_usage\",\"content\":10,\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:43.000Z\"},{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"content\":{\"id\":\"call_00_ET_abWmdvO0m478GbTVgTOH7536\",\"name\":\"execute\",\"args\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/daytona/asyncio_circuit_breaker && python3 -m pytest -q 2>&1 | tail -5\",\"timeout\":120,\"__result\":\"..............................                                           [100%]\\n30 passed in 0.76s\\n\\n[Command succeeded with exit code 0]\"},\"result\":\"..............................                                           [100%]\\n30 passed in 0.76s\\n\\n[Command succeeded with exit code 0]\",\"hasResult\":true},\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:43.000Z\",\"endedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:47.000Z\"},{\"type\":\"tool_call_result\",\"content\":{\"tool_call_id\":\"call_00_ET_abWmdvO0m478GbTVgTOH7536\",\"name\":\"execute\",\"content\":\"..............................                                           [100%]\\n30 passed in 0.76s\\n\\n[Command succeeded with exit code 0]\"},\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:47.000Z\",\"endedAt\":\"2026-08-25T02:48:47.000Z\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":\"All 30 t